  "goodToKnow": "Die Amtszeit is the term of office: Die Amtszeit des Bundespräsidenten beträgt fünf Jahre. A chancellor's term follows the Bundestag's four-year Legislaturperiode, and there's no limit on how many terms they can serve: Angela Merkel and Helmut Kohl each served 16 years. The linking s in Amt-s-zeit is typical of compounds. Das Amt means office, as in das Auswärtige Amt (Foreign Office) and der Amtsantritt (taking office)."
